+Disposition: ready for review
+
+## Outcome
+
+- Added the strict schema-versioned relay asset source contract and generated-manifest schema under `relay/`.
+- Added `scripts/relay_asset_manifest.py`, which validates the accepted upstream archive SHA-256 before parsing, requires the exact ordered four-member regular/executable USTAR set, checks byte size, lowercase SHA-256, Mach-O/ELF tuple headers, embedded relay version/source commit, provenance, and canonical manifest bytes, and rejects missing, extra, renamed, duplicate, zero-length, unsafe, stale, protocol/schema-mismatched, unparseable, and tampered inputs.
+- Deterministically materialized exactly four trusted executables plus `relux-relay-assets-v1.json` under ignored `.build/relay/relay-assets-v1/`. The source is the accepted `TASK-260715-24icoz_portable-relay-assets.tar.gz` resource with archive SHA-256 `1f0ba226ed591d1baf5f9464b33e45b7658a33bf5a1a114e77b6d22d3d9eef4e`; no current-HEAD rebuild was substituted.
+- Added immutable `RelayAssetCatalog.bundled` lookup in `ReluxTunnelCore`, with typed Darwin/Linux and amd64/arm64 tuples, documented `Darwin|macOS|Linux` and `x86_64|amd64|aarch64|arm64` handoff normalization, exact metadata, build identity/provenance, and `Bundle.main` resolution without caller-supplied paths or mutable manifest injection.
+- Generated workspace resources now point only to `.build/relay/relay-assets-v1`. The same generated Core lookup compiled through the SwiftPM iOS/macOS adapter targets and the Tuist-generated macOS provider product.
+- Updated the provider graph validator, workspace generators/validators, Make targets, README tooling table, generated-workspace documentation, and LOGBOOK provenance/anomaly record.
+
+## Trusted asset matrix
+
